    {
      "caseId": "breast_symptoms_001",
      "query": "What are the symptoms of breast cancer?",
      "trace": {
        "sessionId": "bd77c1be-7192-4273-abe7-b3c592ec395d",
        "messageId": "3df115ef-f4c0-4a4c-9e97-5585518a5c12",
        "responseText": "**Important:** This information is for general educational purposes and is not a diagnosis. Please consult with your healthcare provider for accurate, personalized medical information.\n\nI understand you're asking about the symptoms of breast cancer.\n\nIt's important to be aware of changes in your breasts and to discuss them with your doctor . While most breast changes aren't cancer, it's best to get them checked out. Here are some potential signs and symptoms of breast cancer to watch for:\n* A new lump in or near your breast \n* Swelling of the breast \n* Redness or other skin changes \n* Nipple changes \n* Swollen lymph nodes \n\nTo diagnose breast cancer, doctors often use a mammogram, ultrasound, and biopsy.\n\nWhat to do next: If you notice any of these changes, it's important to see a doctor right away. They may recommend a mammogram to investigate further. You can also call the Indian Cancer Society at 1800-22-1951 for support and information. If you experience sudden, severe breast pain or a rapidly growing lump, seek immediate medical attention at your nearest hospital or call 112 or 108 for emergency services.\n\nHave you noticed any specific changes in your breasts that you're concerned about?\n\n---\n*This information is for general educational purposes only and is not a substitute for professional medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. Always consult your healthcare provider for personalized guidance.*",
