    {
      "caseId": "breast_signs_002",
      "query": "What are the early warning signs of breast cancer?",
      "trace": {
        "sessionId": "a87fa5f4-5645-464b-824e-2d13d01e55b4",
        "messageId": "c0a2f913-1f63-406a-ba17-c416df388b5a",
        "responseText": "**Important:** This information is for general educational purposes and is not a diagnosis. Please consult with your healthcare provider for accurate, personalized medical information.\n\nHere are common symptoms described in the medical literature:\n\nI understand you're asking about the early warning signs of breast cancer.\n\nHere's what to look for:\n\n**1) WARNING SIGNS**\n- It's important to check with your doctor if you notice any unusual changes in your breasts .\n- This includes a lump in or near your breast .\n\nSymptoms cannot confirm cancer; confirmation requires medical evaluation and often a biopsy.\n\n**2) HOW DOCTORS CONFIRM**\n- Screening mammograms are an important way to find breast cancer early .\n- Depending on your symptoms, your doctor may suggest that you have a diagnostic mammogram .\n\n**3) WHEN TO SEEK CARE**\nI don't have enough information in my NCI sources to provide a specific timeline. Please consult a clinician for guidance on when to seek care.\n\n**4) QUESTIONS TO ASK THE DOCTOR**\n- What kind of imaging do I need?\n- Do I need a biopsy?\n- What symptoms should I watch out for?\n- What follow-up is needed?\n- If cancer is confirmed, what staging or subtype tests will be done?\n- Where can I go for a second opinion?\n- What are the costs involved in diagnosis and treatment?\n\nIf you notice any unusual changes in your breasts, it is important to check with your doctor . You can also contact the Indian Cancer Society at 1800-22-1951.\n\n**Additional warning signs to be aware of:**\n- Redness \n- Swelling \n\n**Note:** These symptoms can overlap with other conditions and are not specific to any one diagnosis.\n\n---\n*This information is for general educational purposes only and is not a substitute for professional medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. Always consult your healthcare provider for personalized guidance.*",
